@startuml animate-stick-figure-structure
title animate_stick_figure.py — Structure
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Developer / User" as User
package "CLI: main()" {
  [argparse\n--input-jsonl\n--output-html\n--title] as CLI
  [Path validation] as Validate
}
package "Data processing" {
  [load_jsonl(path)] as Load
  [json.loads per line] as Parse
  [landmark_map(record)] as Normalize
  [timestamp sort] as Sort
}
package "HTML generation" {
  [make_html(frames, title)] as HTML
  [JSON serialization\nframes + CONNECTIONS] as Serialize
  [HTML template\nCSS + Canvas + JS] as Template
}
database "Input JSONL\n(read-only)" as Input
file "Output HTML\n(local standalone file)" as Output
cloud "External network" as Network

User --> CLI : command line
CLI --> Validate : resolve paths
Validate --> Input : verify exists
Validate --> Load : valid input
Load --> Input : read UTF-8 lines
Load --> Parse
Parse --> Normalize : each frame record
Normalize --> Sort : normalized landmarks
Sort --> HTML : timestamped frames
HTML --> Serialize
Serialize --> Template
Template --> Output : write_text(UTF-8)
User --> Output : open in browser
Network -[hidden]-> Output
note right of Output
Generated page embeds the frame data.
Browser playback uses Canvas and requestAnimationFrame.
No HTTP calls or uploads are implemented.
end note
note bottom of Normalize
Invalid landmark entries are skipped.
x/y are clamped to 0..1.
end note
@enduml
